course: dictionary
lesson: 11557
title: Anagrams: mixing up letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An anagram is a new word or phrase made by changing the order of the letters of another word. You must use every letter exactly once. «Listen» and «silent» are anagrams: they both have the same six letters, but in a different order.
explain: To solve an anagram, try moving the letters around in your head or on paper. Look for common endings like -ing or -er, and try to find a vowel to start with. If your new word has a letter too many or too few, it is not an anagram yet.
explain: Anagrams are often used in word games, crosswords, spelling bees and puzzles. Sometimes a puzzle gives you the anagram of a name or a hidden word, and your job is to find the original.
fact: An anagram uses the same letters as the original word, each one used exactly once.
fact: «Listen» and «silent» are anagrams of each other.
fact: «Dear» and «read» are anagrams because they both have the letters d, e, a and r.
fact: An anagram can be a phrase too, such as making a phrase from the letters of another phrase.
fact: Anagram puzzles are a good way to practise spelling and to notice patterns in words.
exercise: Which word is an anagram of «stone»? | *tones | stones | stoned | stove
exercise: Which pair of words are anagrams of each other? | happy and sad | *dear and read | bright and light | cat and dog
exercise: Which word is an anagram of «Mary»? | marry | arm | *army | mare
test: Which word uses the letters of «night» exactly once? | night | *thing | nights | tight
test: Why are «listen» and «silent» called anagrams? | *They use the same letters, just in a different order | They both start with the letter L | They mean exactly the same thing | They are both very long words
exam: What is an anagram of «tale»? | *teal | tails | tile | tall
